# Claude Code — session/local state is ignored, shared team assets are tracked.
# Use `.claude/*` (not `.claude/`): git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so a bare `.claude/` makes the negations below unreachable. That is
# how `.claude/workforce.yaml` silently failed to ship — the governance config
# existed locally and was absent in CI (caught by
# tests/unit/tools/claude_hooks/test_config.py::test_repo_config_file_is_valid).
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/workforce.yaml
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/agents/
# Personal overrides and session state stay untracked regardless of the above.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Agentic shared assets (skills/agents) are tracked; session/state is ignored.
# Every other agent workspace is ignored wholesale HERE and nowhere else: each
# of .gemini/ and .serena/ was listed twice, once here and once again ~200 lines
# down under its own heading. Duplicate entries are not harmless — a future edit
# that "removes" one is silently overridden by the copy it did not see.
.agents/*
!.agents/skills/
!.agents/agents/
.gemini/
.gemini_scratch/
.serena/


