# F-034: sqlite is now the default mlflow tracking backend. Covers SQLite's
# WAL-mode sidecar files too (-wal/-shm/-journal), not just the main .db.
#
# Do NOT drop mlruns/ above as "legacy" — verified against a real mlflow
# 3.x run: the SQLAlchemy store keeps its ARTIFACT root at ./mlruns even
# when the database is sqlite and absolute. mlruns/ is therefore still an
# active output path (settings snapshots, per-phase checkpoints), not a
# leftover from the file: backend.
mlflow.db
mlflow.db-wal
mlflow.db-shm
mlflow.db-journal
training/data/sequences.pt
training/data/*.pt
training/data/*.npz
